[center][size=6][b]Riposte[/b][/size]
[size=4]A timing circle for every enemy hit, and a grace period for near-miss dodges and parries[/size]

[b]Steam build 23765773 ready  ·  UE4SS 3.0.1  ·  Lua only, no game files changed[/b][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[b]1. Timing circle[/b]
For every upcoming enemy hit a ring shrinks onto a dot and touches it at the exact moment the hit lands. The discs behind it are the real windows of the targeted character, drawn at the same scale:

[list]
[*][color=#33ff59][b]Green[/b][/color] - parry window
[*][color=#33bfff][b]Blue[/b][/color] - dodge window
[*][color=#ffcc1a][b]Yellow[/b][/color] - the grace window this mod adds
[*][color=#ff7300][b]Orange[/b][/color] - jump attack  ·  [color=#b259ff][b]Purple[/b][/color] - gradient attack
[/list]
[b]Rule: press while the ring is inside the disc of the move you want.[/b] The label under the circle names the move the attack asks for.

[b]2. Grace period[/b]
In vanilla a dodge or parry either cancels the hit or does nothing. This mod adds a window around the game's own window:

[list]
[*]Inside the game's window: unchanged (no damage, counters and rewards as usual)
[*]Up to [b]0.25 s too early[/b]: the hit is reduced before it is applied
[*]Up to [b]0.20 s too late[/b]: the reduced share is handed back as HP
[*]Further out: full damage
[/list]
The reduction is [b]90 %[/b] right at the edge of the game's window and falls in a straight line to [b]0 %[/b] at the far edge.

[list]
[*]A near miss [b]never[/b] triggers a counter attack. Only real parries do.
[*]A jump only counts against jump attacks and a gradient parry only against gradient attacks, as in vanilla.
[*]Buff and Lumina damage are never touched.
[*]The late side cannot bring back a character that already died.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Presets[/b][/size]
Pick one main file, then optionally drop a preset over it (it only replaces [i]riposte_config.lua[/i]).

[list]
[*][b]Standard[/b] (main file) - early 0.25 s, late 0.20 s, max reduction 90 %
[*][b]Forgiving[/b] - early 0.40 s, late 0.30 s, max 95 %, at least 20 % off inside the grace window
[*][b]Strict[/b] - early 0.12 s, late 0.08 s, max 60 %
[*][b]Trainer Only[/b] - timing circle only, damage rules 100 % vanilla
[*][b]Grace Only[/b] - grace period only, no circle
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases]RE-UE4SS[/url] [b]3.0.1 or newer[/b] (tested with 3.0.1 Beta, Git SHA 1ceefac8)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install UE4SS: extract it into [code]Expedition 33\Sandfall\Binaries\Win64\[/code] (next to [i]SandFall-Win64-Shipping.exe[/i]).
[*]Extract this mod into the [b]game folder[/b] ([code]...\steamapps\common\Expedition 33\[/code]). It lands in [code]Sandfall\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\Riposte\[/code].
[*]Start the game. [i]ue4ss\UE4SS.log[/i] should contain [code][Riposte] v1.0.0 loaded[/code].
[/list]
[b]Game Pass:[/b] the Win64 folder is [code]C:\XboxGames\Clair Obscur- Expedition 33\Content\Sandfall\Binaries\WinGDK\[/code]. [i]Not tested on Game Pass.[/i]
[b]Linux / Steam Deck (Proton):[/b] add the launch option [code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dwmapi=n,b" %command%[/code]

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [code]ue4ss\Mods\Riposte\[/code]. Nothing else is changed.

[line]

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
Everything is in [code]ue4ss\Mods\Riposte\Scripts\riposte_config.lua[/code] (plain text, commented). Restart the game after editing.

[list]
[*][b]OuterEarly / OuterLate[/b] - size of the grace window on each side
[*][b]MaxReduction / MinReduction[/b] - how forgiving the edge is
[*][b]VisualOffset[/b] - latency compensation for TVs and wireless controllers (makes the ring arrive earlier; try 0.02 - 0.06)
[*][b]OffsetX / OffsetY, RingSpeed, CoreRadius, colours[/b] - look and position of the circle
[*][b]ForgetKey[/b] - [b]Ctrl+F8[/b] forgets the recorded timing of the current attack (see below)
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]How the timings are known[/b][/size]
Many attacks declare their hit moments in advance; the mod reads them. Some attacks do not. For those the mod [b]records when the hit actually reached you[/b] and uses that the next time the same attack plays (saved in [i]riposte_learned.txt[/i]). So:
[list]
[*]The first time you see such an attack, the circle shows [i]NEW ATTACK - LEARNING TIMING[/i].
[*]If a recording looks wrong, press [b]Ctrl+F8[/b] during (or right after) that attack to re-learn it.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Some melee attacks where the enemy runs to you (for example Volester) land at a slightly different time on each run. The circle can be off by up to ~0.2 s on those. Work in progress.
[*]The very first time a jump attack is seen it may be labelled as a normal attack; it corrects itself on later encounters.
[*]Projectile attacks can be a little off the first time.
[*]The late refund uses the game's normal "set HP". Pictos that block healing can interfere with it.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Easier or Harder Dodge and Parry[/b] and other window-size mods: [b]compatible[/b]. The circle reads the real window of the targeted character, so it follows whatever window size is active.
[*][b]Graded Defense[/b]: don't run both. Riposte replaces it, and both would reduce the same hits.
[*]Other UE4SS mods: compatible unless they hook the same damage functions.
[*]No game files are replaced, so game updates don't break saves. If an update changes the attack data, the mod logs one clear warning instead of failing silently.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Performance[/b][/size]
Outside battle the mod does nothing but one check per frame. In battle the expensive object search runs only when an enemy attack starts, widgets are only updated when they change, and nothing is written to disk mid-fight.

